{% extends '_article.jinja' %}
{% from 'data/pages.jinja' import catalogue %}
{% set article = catalogue['roadmap'] %}
{% block article_body %}
<section aria-labelledby="implemented"><h2 id="implemented">Implemented in the documented source</h2>
<p class="fl-label">Implemented · Release forthcoming</p><ul><li>Worker-backed stream, file, rotation, socket, and HTTP output.</li><li>Named logger hierarchy, restricted configuration, and callback filtering.</li><li>Inline structured fields and scoped context through named loggers.</li><li>Rust log/tracing bridges behind optional features.</li></ul><p>The next assumed release is {{ femto_version }}. These statements describe revision <code>{{ femto_revision[:7] }}</code>, not an already published beta.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="planned"><h2 id="planned">Planned work</h2>
<p class="fl-label">Planned · No delivery date</p><p>Formatter registration, batching, benchmark reporting, and observability integrations need further implementation or evidence. Journald and OpenTelemetry exporters require explicit configuration and platform/sink handling; the Rust tracing bridge is a separate capability.</p><p><a href="{{ source_base }}/docs/roadmap.md">Read the upstream roadmap at the documented revision.</a> Check <a href="{{ repository_url }}/blob/main/docs/roadmap.md">the live roadmap</a> for subsequent progress.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="exploratory"><h2 id="exploratory">What-ifs from the field station</h2>
<p class="fl-label">Exploratory · Design questions</p><h3>Context that follows the task</h3><p>A contextvars-backed scope could keep fields isolated across awaits. It needs cancellation, nesting, and bridge-boundary tests before replacing thread-local context.</p><h3>Batches with an accountable boundary</h3><p>A batch-aware handler could amortize transport cost. Ordering, partial failure, flush barriers, and overflow accounting must remain explicit.</p><h3>A closer instrument view</h3><p>A future inspection surface could expose queue pressure without inventing durability guarantees. Any visualization must report observed counters and their scope.</p><p>The concepts suggest alternative futures. They do not set release promises.</p>
</section>
{% endblock %}
